===Etymology 2===
{{ja-kanjitab|yomi=k|とこ}}

{{IPAfont|⟨to<sub>2</sub>ko<sub>2</sub>⟩}} → {{IPAchar|/toko/}}

From {{inh|ja|ojp|sort=とこ|-}}. Cognate with {{m|ja|所|tr=tokoro||place}}. Attested since at least the {{w|Nara period}}, appearing in the ''{{w|Man'yōshū}}'', completed in 759.<ref name="KDJ">{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}</ref><ref>{{RQ:Manyoshu|20|4331}}, text [https://web.archive.org/web/20211203002026/http://jti.lib.virginia.edu/japanese/manyoshu/Man20Yo.html#4331 here]</ref>

Possibly an ancient compound of {{IPAfont|⟨to<sub>1</sub>⟩}} ({{inh|ja|jpx-pro|sort=と|*to|t=place}}, as in {{m|ja|跡}} {{IPAfont|⟨ato<sub>1</sub>⟩}}, “footprint, track”, from “foot '''place''', where one has stepped”) + {{IPAfont|⟨ko<sub>2</sub>⟩}} (noun-forming suffixing element denoting “place”, as in {{m|ja|ここ}} {{IPAfont|⟨ko<sub>2</sub>ko<sub>2</sub>⟩}}, “here”, from “this '''place'''”).

